<title>AUSTRALIA: Comalco deputy chairman Rayner to retire.</title>
<headline>Comalco deputy chairman Rayner to retire.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminium producer Comalco Ltd said on Friday that deputy chairman Mark Rayner would retire from the board on June 30.  </p>
<p>Comalco is 67 percent owned by Rio Tinto.</p>
<p>Rayner was appointed managing director of Comalco in 1978, chief executive from 1979 until 1989 when he became deputy chairman.</p>
<p>&quot;Mr Rayner had made a substantial contribution to the expansion of Comalco and the development of the aluminium industry. He leaves the board with our best wishes and our deep appreciation for his outstanding contribution,&quot; Comalco chairman Leigh Clifford said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
